WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.110
With a background in pro skateboarding, Jason
Lee made an unexpected mark in Hollywood when

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:10.389
he starred as the comedic antihero Brodie
Bruce in 1995's Kevin Smith-directed cult

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:11.260
hit, Mallrats.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.140
"Alright guys you have your mission.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.360
Go forth, wreak havoc"

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:21.140
Lee then quickly rose through the ranks, appearing
in Chasing Amy, Dogma and Jay and Silent Bob

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:21.820
Strike Back.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.770
Then, from the indxie film world to mainstream
TV, Lee's most prominent role came with NBC's

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.340
comedy hit My Name is Earl which garnered
him multiple award nominations.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.980
A multi-faceted artist, Lee maintained an
actively creative lifestyle after the show

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.940
went off the air.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.140
Here's a closer look at what he's been up
to since he shaved off Earl's mustache.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:43.720
Behind the camera

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.920
In 2003, Lee directed Beck's "Lonesome Tears"
music video.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.140
And it appears the project gave him the freedom
to pursue a career behind the camera.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.480
According to Lee, the Beck video led to the
creation of his 2006 short film The White

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:57.980
Door.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.960
And his partnership with Beck led to his helming
multiple music videos for American folk rock

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:03.800
band, Midlake.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.820
Religion gets personal

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:11.120
Lee married his first wife, actress-photographer
Carmen Llywelyn, in 1995.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:15.460
Throughout their relationship Lee did his
best to keep his wife involved with him in

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.300
the Church of Scientology, but the couple
divorced six years later.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.820
According to a Gawker op-ed from Llywelyn,
the final straw was Lee's Scientology practice.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:29.320
Then in 2001, Lee was linked to actress Beth
Riesgraf.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.940
In 2003, their son Pilot Inspektor was born,
and soon the couple became engaged.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.720
Ultimately, the two never tied the knot, and
it was speculated that Scientology may have

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.440
been the culprit behind their breakup in 2007.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.480
The Chipmunks dynasty

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.820
In 2007, Lee gave a live-action human face
to Dave Seville, the adoptive father to the

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.080
three rodent heroes in Alvin and the Chipmunks.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.440
Lee reprised the role in the accompanying
video game as well.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.980
According to Box Office Mojo the film earned
roughly $361 million worldwide and prompted

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:09.750
three sequels: 2009's Alvin and the Chipmunks:
The Squeakquel, 2011's Alvin and the Chipmunks:

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.860
Chipwrecked, and 2015's Alvin and the Chipmunks:
The Road Chip.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.800
"Alviiiiiin…"

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.980
Jason Lee, voice actor

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:26.720
A year before he started filming My Name is
Earl, Lee appeared as the villainous Syndrome

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.960
in Disney's The Incredibles.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.360
It was the first time the actor flexed his
voiceover chops and it was a slam dunk.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.100
"I'm a new superhero.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.020
I'm Syndrome!"

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.760
Lee has since reprised his role in The Incredibles
video game, the short film Jack-Jack Attack,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.480
and the Disney Infinity video game franchise.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.500
His voice has also been regularly featured
in the animated series We Bare Bears, where

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.940
he plays a Bigfoot named Charlie.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.140
"Golly, would you just look at this place?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.180
Rustic, charming...slick headband by the way"

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.320
A less-than triumphant return

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:04.480
Lee had made a name for himself, playing offbeat
characters, but in 2010, the actor delved

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.620
into procedurals with TNT's short-lived cop
drama, Memphis Beat.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.240
The show, however, wouldn't live to see a
third season.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.500
Lee then quickly moved back to NBC, for a
recurring role on Up All Night in 2011.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.180
He appeared in only seven episodes of the
show, which went on hiatus halfway into season

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.020
2 before being officially canceled by the
network.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.540
Then in 2015, Mallrats director Kevin Smith
announced that a sequel to his cult hit would

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.640
finally see the light of day, tweeting:

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.420
"20 years in the making.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.740
113 pages fulla old friends and new jokes."

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.820
Lee was set to reprise his role in Smith's
new Mallbrats movie, but getting the rights

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.420
from Universal proved to be an epic challenge.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.700
Instead, Smith retooled the project for television
and while it seemed that Brodie would finally

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.120
get his comeback, CinemaBlend reported no
networks showed interested in the project.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.820
Staying true to his roots

00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:02.090
Lee retired from pro skateboarding in '95,
but back in '92, he and fellow pro skateboarder,

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.800
Chris Pastras, had created their own skate
brand, Stereo Skateboards.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.300
After over a decade off the rails, Lee returned
to skating and relaunched the company with

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.380
Pastras in 2003.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:18.620
Combining their love for record collecting,
improvisational jazz, and movie-making, Stereo

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:23.200
has since stood out from the pack with its
unique brand aesthetic and quality boards.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.420
Moving out of Hollywood

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.640
Lee practiced Scientology for more than two
decades.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:35.480
But in 2016, he revealed that he and his second
wife, Ceren Lee, had left Scientology altogether.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.780
The break occurred around the same time the
couple moved to Denton, Texas with their three

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:40.340
children.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.720
Lee told The Dentonite,

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:46.140
"We're not here to buy up or change or take
over Denton, put some kind of personal stamp

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:46.640
on it.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.159
We're just here like anyone else who wants
to be a part of Denton's very cool creative

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:54.220
community, and to be involved and perhaps
help where we can."

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.060
Ever since, Lee has taken on a variety of
off-screen endeavors.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:03.350
And it seems the skateboarder/actor/director/photographer
has found fulfillment in shifting his focus

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.550
from Hollywood's glitz and glam, to doing
what he really loves.

